<title>GERMANY: Deutz 1996 group net profit 874 mln DM.</title>
<headline>Deutz 1996 group net profit 874 mln DM.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless indicated:</p>
<p>    Group net profit		 874 vs 1134 loss</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet loss	78 vs 952 loss</p>
<p>    DVFA loss per share (DM)    1.86 vs 18.99 loss</p>
<p>    EBITDA			     134 vs 918 loss</p>
<p>    Loss carryforward		952 vs 363 loss</p>
<p>    Extraordinary profit	   897 vs 61</p>
<p>    Group loss from ord. act.     19 vs 1187 loss</p>
<p>    Financial loss		    17 vs 39 loss</p>
<p>    Group sales		     2921 vs 3285</p>
<p>    Drawdown from reserves	   0 vs 247</p>
<p>    Capital reduction		  0 vs 298</p>
<p>NOTE - Machinery maker Deutz AG, formerly known as Kloeckner-Humboldt-Deutz AG, was rescued last year by its creditor banks led by Deutsche Bank AG following large losses</p>
<p>in 1995. The company said the bank's contributions accounted for most of the reported extraordinary profit, and that the restructuring had cost 1.008 billion marks. It said it had reduced its net debt to 602 million marks by the end of 1996 from 1.023 billion marks a year earlier, and that it had capital of 220 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
